Package: SimLev
Type: Package
Title: Simulation and Backtesting with German Investment Taxation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("ChemicalStats", "von der Mauerstrasse",
                  role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
                  email = "chemicalstatsy@protonmail.com")
Description: A fast/slow-path backtesting engine for leveraged and unleveraged ETF and
    multi-asset strategies. Supports calendar- and event-based rebalancing,
    dollar-cost averaging, asset splits, and a detailed model of German
    investment taxation including Vorabpauschale, Teilfreistellung and the
    loss-offset rules of sections 20 and 23 of the EStG. Performance-critical
    market updates are implemented in C++ via 'Rcpp'.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0)
Imports: Rcpp, stats, graphics, grDevices
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), knitr, rmarkdown, plotly, TTR
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
RoxygenNote: 7.3.1
NeedsCompilation: yes
